# Git: SSH only

## Hard ban

- **NEVER** use `https://github.com/...` (or any HTTPS git URL) for `git remote`, `git push`, `git fetch`, `git pull`, `git ls-remote`, or one-off push URLs.
- **NEVER** run `git remote add` / `git remote set-url` with an `https://` URL.
- **NEVER** “work around” SSH failures by switching to HTTPS. If SSH fails (`Permission denied (publickey)`), **stop** and tell the user. Do not invent an HTTPS fallback.
- After any remote change, verify with `git remote -v` that every URL is `git@github.com:...` (or other `git@` / `ssh://` form).

## Allowed

- `git@github.com:DevNathan/ftl-dev.git`
- `git@github.com:DevNathan/ftl-dev.vim.git` (remote name: `vim-publish`)
- Documented **user-facing** clone URLs in README may stay HTTPS for humans; agent operations still use SSH.

